IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fraud-nouns`
IMPORT `fraud-dates`
IMPORT `fraud-s15`
IMPORT `fraud-penalty`
IMPORT `fraud-s01-s05`
IMPORT `fraud-s06-s08`
IMPORT `fraud-s09`
IMPORT `fraud-s11`

-- Fraud Act 2006: TESTS FOR THE DATES, SECTION 15 AND THE PENALTY SUBSECTIONS.
--
-- Expected values come from the text and are written beside each assertion.  The "appointed day"
-- used in the section 15(1) tests is a made-up date, chosen only to test either side of it: the
-- Act leaves the real day to an order, which is not among the sources.

§ `Tests for the dates, section 15 and the penalties`

§§ `The dates the text fixes`

-- src:4 "[8th November 2006]".  Written here with the day first, so the test does not lean on the YMD shim.
#ASSERT `the date of enactment of the Fraud Act 2006` EQUALS Date 8 11 2006
-- src:344 "2 May 2022".
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 1: the date from which the general limit is not read as 6 months` EQUALS Date 2 5 2022
-- The shim reads year first.
#ASSERT YearMonthDay 2022 5 2 EQUALS Date 2 5 2022

§§ `Section 15(1): commencement by order`

-- No day appointed: the Act (except sections 15 and 16) is not yet in force.
#ASSERT NOT `section 15(1): the Act is in force for a purpose on` NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1)
-- A day appointed (made-up: 1 March 2007): in force on that day, not the day before, and after.
#ASSERT `section 15(1): the Act is in force for a purpose on` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2007 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2007 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 15(1): the Act is in force for a purpose on` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2007 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2007 2 28)
#ASSERT `section 15(1): the Act is in force for a purpose on` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2007 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2007 3 2)

§§ `Section 15(2) and (3): extent`

-- s 15(2): England and Wales and Northern Ireland only.
#ASSERT `section 15(2): sections 1 to 9 and 11 to 13 extend to` `England`
#ASSERT `section 15(2): sections 1 to 9 and 11 to 13 extend to` `Wales`
#ASSERT `section 15(2): sections 1 to 9 and 11 to 13 extend to` `Northern Ireland`
#ASSERT NOT `section 15(2): sections 1 to 9 and 11 to 13 extend to` `Scotland`
#ASSERT NOT `section 15(2): sections 1 to 9 and 11 to 13 extend to` `anywhere else`
-- s 15(3): section 8 so far as it relates to the Armed Forces Act 2001 extends where that Act extends.
#ASSERT `section 15(3): section 8, so far as it relates to the Armed Forces Act 2001, extends to the place` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 15(3): section 8, so far as it relates to the Armed Forces Act 2001, extends to the place` FALSE

§§ `Schedule 2 paragraph 1 and the Northern Ireland reading`

-- Para 1: "committed before 2 May 2022".  The day before, the day itself, the day after.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 1: the offence was committed before 2 May 2022` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 1: the offence was committed before 2 May 2022` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 2)
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 1: the offence was committed before 2 May 2022` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 3)
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 1: the offence was committed before 2 May 2022` (YearMonthDay 2007 1 1)
-- ss 1(4) etc.: only Northern Ireland.
#ASSERT `sections 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7) and 11(4): in Northern Ireland the limit on summary conviction is read as 6 months` `Northern Ireland`
#ASSERT NOT `sections 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7) and 11(4): in Northern Ireland the limit on summary conviction is read as 6 months` `England`
#ASSERT NOT `sections 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7) and 11(4): in Northern Ireland the limit on summary conviction is read as 6 months` `Wales`

-- The longest term on summary conviction: England before the date, on the date, after it.
#ASSERT `sections 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a) and 11(3)(a): the longest term on summary conviction` `England` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1) EQUALS `six months`
#ASSERT `sections 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a) and 11(3)(a): the longest term on summary conviction` `England` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 2) EQUALS `the general limit in a magistrates' court (the Act states no figure)`
#ASSERT `sections 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a) and 11(3)(a): the longest term on summary conviction` `Wales` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1) EQUALS `six months`
#ASSERT `sections 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a) and 11(3)(a): the longest term on summary conviction` `Wales` (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) EQUALS `the general limit in a magistrates' court (the Act states no figure)`
-- Northern Ireland: six months whatever the date (s 1(4) reading, F2; before the date also by para 1).
#ASSERT `sections 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a) and 11(3)(a): the longest term on summary conviction` `Northern Ireland` (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) EQUALS `six months`
#ASSERT `sections 1(3)(a), 6(2)(a), 7(2)(a), 9(6)(a) and 11(3)(a): the longest term on summary conviction` `Northern Ireland` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1) EQUALS `six months`

§§ `The penalty for each offence`

GIVEN limit IS A `Summary imprisonment limit`
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`the penalty the text states, with` limit years MEANS JUST (`Penalty` WITH
    `on summary conviction, imprisonment for a term not exceeding` IS limit
    `on summary conviction, a fine not exceeding` IS `the statutory maximum (the Act states no figure)`
    `on conviction on indictment, imprisonment for a term not exceeding, in years` IS years
    `on conviction on indictment, a fine not exceeding` IS `no limit is stated`
    `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS TRUE)

`the general limit` MEANS `the general limit in a magistrates' court (the Act states no figure)`

-- s 1(3): fraud.  Summary: the general limit or the statutory maximum or both; on indictment: 10 years or a fine or both.
#ASSERT `section 1(3): the penalty for fraud` `England` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `the general limit` 10
#ASSERT `section 1(3): the penalty for fraud` `Wales` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 2) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `the general limit` 10
#ASSERT `section 1(3): the penalty for fraud` `England` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `six months` 10
#ASSERT `section 1(3): the penalty for fraud` `Northern Ireland` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `six months` 10
-- s 15(2): not extended to Scotland or anywhere else, so the Act states no penalty there.
#ASSERT `section 1(3): the penalty for fraud` `Scotland` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 1(3): the penalty for fraud` `anywhere else` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(2): possession etc.: 5 years on indictment.
#ASSERT `section 6(2): the penalty for possession etc. of articles for use in frauds` `England` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `the general limit` 5
#ASSERT `section 6(2): the penalty for possession etc. of articles for use in frauds` `Northern Ireland` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `six months` 5
#ASSERT `section 6(2): the penalty for possession etc. of articles for use in frauds` `Scotland` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(2): making or supplying: 10 years on indictment.
#ASSERT `section 7(2): the penalty for making or supplying articles for use in frauds` `Wales` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `the general limit` 10
#ASSERT `section 7(2): the penalty for making or supplying articles for use in frauds` `England` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `six months` 10
-- s 9(6): participating in fraudulent business: 10 years on indictment.
#ASSERT `section 9(6): the penalty for participating in fraudulent business carried on by sole trader etc.` `England` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `the general limit` 10
#ASSERT `section 9(6): the penalty for participating in fraudulent business carried on by sole trader etc.` `Northern Ireland` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `six months` 10
-- s 11(3): obtaining services dishonestly: 5 years on indictment.
#ASSERT `section 11(3): the penalty for obtaining services dishonestly` `England` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `the general limit` 5
#ASSERT `section 11(3): the penalty for obtaining services dishonestly` `Northern Ireland` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `six months` 5
-- The shared shape, with a made-up number of years, shows the number flows through.
#ASSERT `the penalty subsection: what may follow conviction` 7 `England` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS `the penalty the text states, with` `the general limit` 7
